{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017qSoRBtAZ2e1Yc4SpSHW49","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed as `8164b9f`. Ralph infra files (`.ralph/`, `.ralphrc`) untouched.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis loop I completed the next pending autonomous task: **Pro Mode denser spectrum**.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Confirmed only the Goniometer half of Pro Mode had landed — `SpectrumDisplay` ignored `proMode` and rendered identically in both modes.\n2. Added a `pro` prop to `SpectrumDisplay`, wired from `proMode` at the /master call site.\n3. Pro mode now renders a **denser 10-point frequency grid with vertical gridlines** (`20/50/100/200/500/1k/2k/5k/10k/20k`) vs. the sparse 6-label standard set (`20/100/1k/5k/10k/20k`).\n4. Extracted the density decision into the pure `spectrumDensity` helper so the \"pro is strictly denser\" property is unit-testable without canvas.\n5. Null-guarded the 2D context (mirroring Goniometer), fixing a latent crash risk and making the component renderable under jsdom.\n6. Added `data-testid`/`data-pro` for observability + a component smoke test.\n\n**Green gate:** `tsc` clean, `eslint .` clean, 7/7 new tests passing.\n\n**Genuinely remaining autonomous task:** Extract the `MasterScreen` component (mode prop) from the inline mode-switch in `src/app/master/page.tsx` — the last item in the Direction-A batch.\n\n```\n---RALPH_STATUS---\nSTATUS: IN_PROGRESS\nTASKS_COMPLETED_THIS_LOOP: 1\nFILES_MODIFIED: 6\nTESTS_STATUS: PASSING\nWORK_TYPE: IMPLEMENTATION\nEXIT_SIGNAL: false\nRECOMMENDATION: Next loop, extract the MasterScreen component (mode prop) from the inline mode-switch in src/app/master/page.tsx with an RTL test — the last remaining autonomous item.\n---END_RALPH_STATUS---\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":127596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemer